# Important technical note

IronPDF’s tutorial currently shows this memory setup:

```csharp
var memory = new MemoryBuilder()
    .WithMemoryStore(new VolatileMemoryStore())
    .WithAzureOpenAITextEmbeddingGeneration(embeddingDeployment, azureEndpoint, apiKey)
    .Build();
```

([IronPDF][1])

Do **not** use that exact line in this project.

You already hit the compile error because `MemoryBuilder.WithAzureOpenAITextEmbeddingGeneration(...)` is not available in your current package/API combination.

Also, Microsoft’s Semantic Kernel guidance says embedding workflows are moving from older SK embedding abstractions toward `Microsoft.Extensions.AI.IEmbeddingGenerator<string, Embedding<float>>`. Your branch already uses that newer abstraction for embeddings and vector search. ([Microsoft Learn][2])

So the clean project-specific solution is:

> Use the existing centralized `IEmbeddingGenerator<string, Embedding<float>>`, adapt it only where IronPDF requires Semantic Kernel memory, and keep that compatibility code isolated inside `KnowledgeOps.AI`.

