# Step 8 — Replace `CreatePreview` with `CreatePreviewAsync`

Current method:

```csharp
private string? CreatePreview(string rawText)
{
    if (rawText.Length <= PreviewLength)
    {
        return rawText;
    }

    return rawText[..PreviewLength] + "...";
}
```

Replace it with:

```csharp
private async Task<string?> CreatePreviewAsync(
    PortalDocument document,
    PdfDocument pdf,
    string rawText,
    CancellationToken cancellationToken)
{
    cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();

    try
    {
        ironPdfAiInitializer.EnsureInitialized();

        logger.LogInformation(
            "Generating IronPDF AI summary for document {DocumentId}.",
            document.Id);

        string summary = await pdf.Summarize();

        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(summary))
        {
            string normalizedSummary = NormalizeExtractedText(summary);

            logger.LogInformation(
                "IronPDF AI summary generated for document {DocumentId}. Summary length: {SummaryLength}.",
                document.Id,
                normalizedSummary.Length);

            return normalizedSummary;
        }

        logger.LogWarning(
            "IronPDF AI summary returned empty content for document {DocumentId}. Falling back to text preview.",
            document.Id);
    }
    catch (Exception exception)
    {
        logger.LogError(
            exception,
            "IronPDF AI summary failed for document {DocumentId}. Falling back to text preview.",
            document.Id);
    }

    return CreateTextPreview(rawText);
}
```

Now add this small private helper:

```csharp
private string? CreateTextPreview(string rawText)
{
    if (rawText.Length <= PreviewLength)
    {
        return rawText;
    }

    return rawText[..PreviewLength] + "...";
}
```

## Why add this helper?

This keeps `CreatePreviewAsync` focused:

```text
Try AI summary
Fallback to old preview logic
```

The fallback logic remains clear and reusable.

This is not unnecessary abstraction. It keeps the old preview behavior intact and makes the new async method easier to read.

